{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-04-01T07:10:47.174494+00:00", "modified": "2026-04-01T07:10:47.410358+00:00", "id": 19364950, "conceptrecid": "19364949", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19364950", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19364949", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19364950", "metadata": {"title": "CharithaPalika/BasalGanglia_DBS_model: Harnessing DBS to improve Exploration and Optimize Decision-Making through STN-GPe Desynchronization", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19364950", "publication_date": "2026-04-01", "description": "<p>\ud83d\ude80 Release: Initial Version (v1.0)</p>\n<p>This release provides the first stable version of the Basal Ganglia &amp; STN\u2013GPe Simulation Workspace, developed for studying neural dynamics, decision-making, and stimulation strategies in Parkinson's disease.</p>\n<p>\ud83d\udd2c Overview</p>\n<p>The repository integrates computational neuroscience and dynamical systems modeling to investigate how basal ganglia circuits and STN\u2013GPe dynamics influence behavior under normal, Parkinsonian, and Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS) conditions. In addition, it includes simulations of standard 130 Hz DBS, closed-loop DBS, and a novel open-loop stimulation protocol, enabling comparison of their effects on network synchronization and decision-making performance.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Palika Charitha", "affiliation": null}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/CharithaPalika/BasalGanglia_DBS_model/tree/basal-ganglia-DBS", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "basal-ganglia-DBS", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/CharithaPalika/BasalGanglia_DBS_model"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "19364949"}}]}}, "title": "CharithaPalika/BasalGanglia_DBS_model: Harnessing DBS to improve Exploration and Optimize Decision-Making through STN-GPe Desynchronization", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19364950", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19364950?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19364950", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19364950", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19364950", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364949", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19364949", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19364949", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19364949", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19364950/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19364950/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19364950/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/requests"}, "updated": "2026-04-01T07:10:47.410358+00:00", "recid": "19364950", "revision": 3, "files": [{"id": "8be07ff9-73b1-49fb-bac7-4b05621a67d3", "key": "CharithaPalika/BasalGanglia_DBS_model-basal-ganglia-DBS.zip", "size": 37375030, "checksum": "md5:2666941bf1991824bd558d73ffc775dd", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19364950/files/CharithaPalika/BasalGanglia_DBS_model-basal-ganglia-DBS.zip/content"}}], "swh": {"swhid": "swh:1:dir:1de7edd178daf9a23dfc9b9fdd54b80e6d2d9d5a;origin=https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19364949;visit=swh:1:snp:12793b72eb0faa5503bf2546a972f5c24867f9f8;anchor=swh:1:rel:0efe703b7ff503f04d4a63bd150aa4a02ba83536;path=CharithaPalika-BasalGanglia_DBS_model-95e0c32"}, "owners": [{"id": "1397010"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 10, "unique_downloads": 9, "views": 19, "unique_views": 19, "version_downloads": 10, "version_unique_downloads": 9, "version_unique_views": 19, "version_views": 19}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-07-14T07:09:12.756710+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-14T07:18:05.458425+00:00", "id": 21351821, "conceptrecid": "21351820", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21351821", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21351820", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21351821", "metadata": {"title": "Adaptive Motor Control Through Utility-Based Arbitration Between Basal Ganglia and Cerebellum", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21351821", "publication_date": "2026-07-14", "description": "<p><span>In this work, we have proposed a utility-based architecture that enables continuous arbitration between the basal ganglia (BG) and the cerebellum (CB) in uncertain motor environments, where BG and CB dominate under unpredictable and predictable settings, respectively. <br><br>The BG is implemented using a utility framework that balances value and risk, where a risk network estimates the variance of the temporal-difference error. CB is modeled as a feedforward network to imitate the learned policy. Motor commands are generated as a weighted combination of CB and BG outputs, with weights &alpha; and (1&minus;&alpha;), respectively. &alpha; is generated by a neural network that evaluates utility, increasing CB contribution when utility is high and shifting control toward BG when utility is low. The environment is perturbed through a visuomotor rotation that alters visual feedback of the target and fingertip positions. <br><br>The results show that BG contribution is higher in moments of higher uncertainty (early phase and when the environment is perturbed), and CB contribution is higher when there is low uncertainty in the environment. The framework explains how control can be redistributed between BG and CB according to task performance and uncertainty.</span></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Aditya Shreeram", "affiliation": "Indian Institute of Technology Madras", "orcid": "0009-0002-2438-9527"}, {"name": "Palika, Charitha", "affiliation": "Indian Institute of Technology Madras", "orcid": "0009-0003-8957-793X"}, {"name": "Chakravarthy, Srinivasa", "affiliation": "Indian Institute of Technology Madras", "orcid": "0000-0002-2453-1637"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Conference proceeding", "type": "publication", "subtype": "conferenceproceeding"}, "meeting": {"title": "Neurogati Summer School 2026", "dates": "20 June 2026", "place": "Online"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "neurogati_summer_school_2026"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21351820"}}]}}, "title": "Adaptive Motor Control Through Utility-Based Arbitration Between Basal Ganglia and Cerebellum", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21351821", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21351821", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21351821?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zeno